WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office Ladies.

8
00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:24.380
Hello, everybody.

9
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:25.540
Good morning.

10
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:26.480
Or afternoon.

11
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.400
It's morning for us.

12
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.300
Or good evening.

13
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.700
We don't know when you listen.

14
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:30.500
We don't.

15
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:31.960
Although I'm always fascinated.

16
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.780
I love it when people share where they listen and when and what they're doing.

17
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:36.560
I just love it.

18
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:38.720
A lot of people listen while they do chores.

19
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:39.500
Yeah.

20
00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:40.300
Mm-hmm.

21
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.020
I think that's a good time to listen.

22
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:42.560
I do, too.

23
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.080
I had one gal say she sneaks and listens at work.

24
00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:45.860
Oh.

25
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:47.300
What does she do?

26
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:48.440
I don't know.

27
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.560
I should always do the follow-up question.

28
00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:51.660
Mm-hmm.

29
00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.040
Don't know what you do at work.

30
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.340
But thanks for listening to us.

31
00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.540
I hope everything else in your office is safely going about its business.

32
00:00:58.800 --> 00:00:59.000
Yes.

33
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.400
I hope you're having a good day at work.

34
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:00.720
Mm-hmm.

35
00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.140
Today is Lecture Circuit Part 2.

36
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.420
It is Season 5, Episode 17.

37
00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.580
Written by Mindy Kaling and directed by Ken Quappas.

38
00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.000
Here's a summary.

39
00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.520
Pam and Michael are still on their speaking tour.

40
00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:23.220
Because remember, Michael was asked by David Wallace to tell all the other branches how to be as successful as Scranton.

41
00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:23.620
Mm-hmm.

42
00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:25.960
Well, they've decided to take a detour.

43
00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:32.560
They're going to add Nashua to the Lecture Circuit so that Michael can see Holly and get some closure.

44
00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.480
And Pam is all about it.

45
00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:35.700
Pam's up for it.

46
00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:36.060
Yeah.

47
00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:37.240
But guess what?

48
00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:37.640
What?

49
00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:38.740
Holly's not there.

50
00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:39.740
Oh, no.

51
00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:40.860
You know who is there?

52
00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:42.040
AJ.

53
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:43.660
Holly's new boyfriend.

54
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.240
New boyfriend?

55
00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:45.980
Oof.

56
00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:51.720
Back in Scranton, Jim and Dwight are still trying to do right by Kelly's missed birthday.

57
00:01:52.280 --> 00:02:00.640
And Angela has a very new expensive cat that she bought with the money from selling her engagement ring from Andy.

58
00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:04.780
And she has to keep tabs on it with a whole video system.

59
00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.280
Not even just keep tabs.

60
00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.600
She's delighted to just watch her cats while she's at work.

61
00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.500
That's what she's doing while she's at work.

62
00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:12.740
Yeah, exactly.

63
00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.260
Well, fast fact number one.

64
00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:23.480
If you listened last week, then you'll remember that we explained how Lecture Circuit was originally meant to be a single episode.

65
00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:29.160
But when they got to the editing room, it was just so good, they decided to turn it into two.

66
00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:30.100
Yeah.

67
00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.860
Jenna, weren't you so surprised when you started watching this one?

68
00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:39.160
And even though I knew that information, because we talked about that last week, on the screen it said previously on The Office.

69
00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:39.860
Yes.

70
00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.680
And then there was a whole recap.

71
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.220
Never seen that before.

72
00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:43.660
Never.

73
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.840
Not very documentary, is it?

74
00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:46.980
Not very documentary.

75
00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:52.640
Well, they had to add extra stories in order to make it two episodes.

76
00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:57.320
Remember last week they had the story of Andy trying to date Stanley's client?

77
00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:03.380
Well, this week, the extra storyline is all about Angela and her cats.

78
00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:04.180
Oh, yeah.

79
00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.700
Angela, I texted with Mindy about this.

80
00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:07.180
You did?

81
00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:07.900
I did.

82
00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:08.840
What did she say?

83
00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:16.560
She said she thought that on paper that that cat storyline was a little broad and a little silly.

84
00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.060
But here was a thing that the writers knew about you, Angela.

85
00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:21.640
What?

86
00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.140
And this is something that Jen Salata said.

87
00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:31.420
Remember back in the duel that you do such a great job of grounding comedy and making it work.

88
00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:37.480
And so they could just throw these broader storylines at you and you made them sing.

89
00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:38.920
She said, what a gift.

90
00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.820
Let me tell you something.

91
00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.300
I am on cloud nine right now.

92
00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.200
I am absolutely giddy.

93
00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.900
Mindy and Jen Salata's opinion of my acting and comedic skills mean more to me than any award.

94
00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:51.720
You heard me.

95
00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:55.440
I will take this Mindy and Jen award to my heart.

96
00:03:55.700 --> 00:04:01.540
I'm going to make you a little mini Jen and a little mini Mindy statue and give them to you.

97
00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.120
Is that weird if I have a miniature statue?

98
00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:09.020
Okay, Mindy and Jen, if you hear this, it's because I so highly regard your opinion.

99
00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:10.960
You just won a Mindy today.

100
00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:11.760
Oh!

101
00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.220
And on the duel, you won a Jen.

102
00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.100
Thank you.

103
00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:18.860
I'd like to thank the Academy of Badass Women for believing in me.

104
00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:22.700
Fast fact number two is a location breakdown.

105
00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.400
Let's discuss the Nashua branch.

106
00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.360
I was really hoping you would.

107
00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.080
Everyone's curious because we did not go to Nashua.

108
00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:36.640
We filmed the exterior and interior scenes at different places.

109
00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:38.500
Mm-hmm.

110
00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:46.460
The exterior of the Nashua branch was actually T&R drywall in Van Nuys.

111
00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:47.400
Huh.

112
00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:48.020
Yep.

113
00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.660
Then we relocated to get this.

114
00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:53.540
Where?

115
00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.020
For the interior scenes.

116
00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:55.320
Where?

117
00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.440
M&M Paper Company.

118
00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:59.440
A real paper company!

119
00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.040
That's amazing!

120
00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:01.720
Right?

121
00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:02.580
Yeah!

122
00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.740
We shot all of the scenes for Nashua at the very end of the week.

123
00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.060
It was on a Friday.

124
00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:14.920
And the very last thing we shot was Steve cutting the sleeve off Holly's sweater.

125
00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:15.380
Oh!

126
00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:16.860
That was the last thing.

127
00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:21.840
But here's something else that we shot that day that I found fascinating.

128
00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:25.980
Here's a little bit of, like, I don't know, is this movie magic?

129
00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:27.380
Something...

130
00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:28.680
Well, you tell me and I'll tell you.

131
00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:29.520
Insidery Hollywood?

132
00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:30.200
Yeah, tell me.

133
00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:32.420
We shot a background plate.

134
00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:35.900
Oh, that's very insidery Hollywood-y movie magic-y.

135
00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:36.460
Yes!

136
00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:37.140
Thank you!

137
00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:37.780
Okay, good.

138
00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:44.560
So a background plate is a shot that they could put behind a future talking head that might

139
00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.000
take place in Nashua.

140
00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.420
So it's just like an empty background.

141
00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.560
And they could superimpose a person there with a green screen.

142
00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:57.580
So if AJ or Holly or anyone from the Nashua branch had a talking head in a future episode,

143
00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:00.220
we wouldn't have to rent this whole building again.

144
00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:03.820
They could just shoot it on a green screen and add our background plate.

145
00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:05.440
It is really cool.

146
00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.320
I've only worked with the background plate one time.

147
00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:10.840
It's for a TV show I shot this year.

148
00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:12.140
I don't know if I can say it yet.

149
00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.220
But we had to be driving through Los Angeles.

150
00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:17.380
And we were in a car, Jenna, on a rig.

151
00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:18.820
And it would move.

152
00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:19.300
Yes!

153
00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.380
Was this sort of like curved screen of like the streets of Los Angeles.

154
00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:28.820
And I got dizzy.

155
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.820
This is the thing you don't think about in acting school, which is you're going to do

156
00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:37.200
a fakie car scene with fakie street going by.

157
00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:40.360
And it might make you a little dizzy if you're prone to that.

158
00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:43.480
Now, could you see the fake street on the screen?

159
00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.000
No, it was surrounding us.

160
00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:46.580
Wow.

161
00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:50.040
Like, you know, one of those fancy movie theaters where the screen goes around you?

162
00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:50.420
I don't know.

163
00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:51.300
They have those, don't they?

164
00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:52.400
Yeah, I think so.

165
00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:52.880
Not somewhere.

166
00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:54.060
Something like that?

167
00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:54.360
Yeah.

168
00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.040
It like went around us.

169
00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:59.260
So we would look out the car window and there'd be the street driving by.

170
00:06:59.540 --> 00:06:59.940
Wow.

171
00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.520
Not the street driving by.

172
00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:02.420
You know what I mean?

173
00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.160
I knew what you meant.

174
00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:08.160
I did a fakie driving scene like that in a studio as well, except it was just a green

175
00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.440
screen and they inserted the images later.

176
00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.860
But I was on a little thing where they make the car move.

177
00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:14.500
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

178
00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:18.700
And it's fans blowing in through the windows for motion.

179
00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:19.160
Yes!

180
00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:19.560
Yeah.

181
00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:26.400
Because that's some of the stuff as a kid that was fascinating to me.

182
00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:26.900
Yeah.

183
00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.100
The fakie movie magic.

184
00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:30.360
It's also like so fascinating.

185
00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.540
Sorry, guys, to go off on a total tangent here.

186
00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:37.120
But to see that many different departments working to pull off one moment.

187
00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:37.480
Yeah.

188
00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:38.880
I always think that's so cool.

189
00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:39.260
Yeah.

190
00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:42.760
All right, Angela, this next location breakdown is all you.

191
00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:49.580
Will you please tell us where was Angela's apartment such that we could see all your cats

192
00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:50.160
on camera?

193
00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.260
Oh, will I?

194
00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.440
I have a whole cat camera location breakdown.

195
00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.580
And then later, Jenna, I have a cat guest star breakdown.

196
00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:00.380
Oh, I can't wait for that.

197
00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:01.380
You will not want to miss it.

198
00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:02.100
All right.

199
00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:05.480
So, you guys, Angela's living room was built on stage two.

200
00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:07.660
That was inside our warehouse set.

201
00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.340
Remember the warehouse where we go?

202
00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:10.360
Yes, of course.

203
00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:10.760
Okay.

204
00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:13.840
We would build a lot of those swing sets.

205
00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:14.420
Yeah.

206
00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:16.020
Little term for you.

207
00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:17.960
They shot the scenes individually.

208
00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:21.940
And then later, they took the one scene with all the cats and they burned that into the

209
00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:22.680
computer screen.

210
00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:27.500
They also burned into the computer screen at my desk the one of me with the cats.

211
00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:28.680
Does that make sense?

212
00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:29.640
A little bit.

213
00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:35.340
So, you filmed it far prior to when you did the scenes at your desk.

214
00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.720
Because then, what does burning it onto your computer screen mean?

215
00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:40.920
I think that's the term Randy used.

216
00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.480
I think it just means uploading it, right?

217
00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:47.420
In post-production, they were able to take the clips and put them on my computer so that

218
00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:49.120
Kevin and Oscar really watched those.

219
00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:51.380
Oh, so they didn't have to imagine what they were seeing.

220
00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:51.600
No.

221
00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:53.020
They really got to watch that.

222
00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:54.280
How delicious was that?

223
00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:58.940
Also, when we all gathered around to watch the cats on the screen, you know, when it's

224
00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:01.780
Meredith and the whole gang, we're really watching the cats.

225
00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:02.400
Oh, okay.

226
00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:03.600
That's amazing.

227
00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:06.140
So, you were really just over in our warehouse set.

228
00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:06.700
That's right.

229
00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:07.920
I worked all day in the warehouse.

230
00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:11.940
Many times when you went to Angela's apartment, even years later, when you went to Oscar's

231
00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:13.520
apartment, that was all in the warehouse.

232
00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:14.260
Wow.

233
00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:16.620
The interior shots, I should say.

234
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:17.180
Yes.

235
00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:20.920
Fast fact number three, we have a big guest star alert.

236
00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:21.840
We do.

237
00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:26.160
It's AJ, Holly's boyfriend, played by Rob Hubel.

238
00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:26.740
Yeah.

239
00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:32.920
Now, Rob is a very successful improviser, actor, writer, Emmy-nominated producer.

240
00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:35.200
He's like a quadruple threat.

241
00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:36.820
That is four.

242
00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:37.620
Yeah.

243
00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:38.600
A double-double threat?

244
00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:39.960
Yeah, he's a double-double threat.

245
00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:43.660
He's been in over 140 films and television shows.

246
00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:44.500
Good Lord.

247
00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:48.380
He was very recently in Transparent with Melora Hardin.

248
00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.260
A little office reunion there.

249
00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:51.740
And Angela, you know Rob.

250
00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:52.920
I do know Rob.

251
00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:57.160
I mean, I met him a long time ago through our mutual friend, Rachel Harris, who later

252
00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:58.880
plays Angela Martin's sister.

253
00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:01.280
It's that little, like, L.A.

254
00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.700
comedy club circle, you know, between the Groundlings and

255
00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.420
improv and stuff.

256
00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:06.540
Rob is very funny.

257
00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:11.200
He's also just delightful to talk to because he's just one of these people to me, kind of

258
00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:14.000
like Will Ferrell, who's just walks into the room funny.

259
00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:14.960
He's friendly.

260
00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:15.940
And he's friendly.

261
00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:16.260
Yeah.

262
00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:19.380
So I knew this episode was coming up and I was like, we got to reach out to Rob.

263
00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:22.420
We need to hear his story about how he came to be on The Office.

264
